+### Routing demand and decision evidence
+
+All routes use the existing Management API authentication. `PUT /channel-groups/:id/routing-demand` accepts `{ groups?, inputs, capacity?, replaceSources }`. `groups` is the complete sorted scheduling scope of at most 32 enabled duplicate groups with the same channel name, including `:id`; omitted means only `:id`. Account references must be current credential IDs in that scope. Each of at most 12 inputs carries a provider, nullable model scope, revision, calculation/expiry timestamps, uncensored history coverage and one or two separately calibrated weekly/five-hour demand windows. Observed-burn inputs have Low confidence and a null upper band. Replacement atomically clears only the named `history-forecast` or `observed-quota-burn` sources, including an empty replacement. Capacity outlooks require the same forecast revision and exact nullable model scope; an uncertain uncalibrated result has no advice or attention. Invalid scope, membership, bounds or evidence returns 400 without replacing accepted state.
+
+`GET /channel-groups/:id/routing-decisions?groups=1,2&limit=20&before=<sequence>` returns `{ current, decisions, capacity, next, retention }`. The optional group scope follows the same rule; `limit` is 1..50 and `before` is the returned opaque pagination cursor. Current targets are recomputed without selecting an account and include calculation/expiry times and explicit account-window scope. Decisions include configured/effective strategy, evidence revision, quota, targets, weights, bypass/fallback reason, admission attempts and the final admitted credential. No request body, session ID, API key or credential secret is retained. The private response uses credential IDs; an authenticated product adapter must apply its own account-inspection authority before returning it publicly. History is a runtime-only ring bounded by 256 decisions, 4 MiB and 24 hours. `retention` reports the retained interval, truncation and restart boundary; it is not durable audit storage. Current snapshots also expire at the relevant quota resets.
+
+`DELETE /channel-groups/:id/routing-demand?groups=1,2&source=history-forecast` clears that source and its outlooks for the exact scope; `observed-quota-burn` is the other accepted source. Demand, outlooks and decision history clear on Home restart. Missing or expired demand never gates dispatch: quota-deadline uses explicit deadline-rate targets, while unknown or expired quota ranks balance. Existing affinity, funding, model gates and final admission remain authoritative.
+
 ### DELETE `/channel-groups/:id`
 
 Soft-deletes the group and its details, and atomically removes its ID from API key `channels` and model group detail `channels`, including soft-deleted records. Other bindings, key identity, and user ownership are preserved. Removing the last API key channel binding makes credential selection unrestricted by that key; removing the last model-detail channel binding restores inheritance from the key. A config event is published when bindings change, and the local runtime config is refreshed. Disabled groups are not removed.
